What the script does
- Finds all .txt files under /workspace/reports/ (by default, recursive).
- Skips symlinks for safety and stores files inside the zip using paths relative to the reports 
directory.
- Writes the archive as reports_<DATE>.zip (DATE is YYYY-MM-DD).
- Writes atomically (temporary file then replace) into /workspace/archives/.
- Uses ZIP_DEFLATED when zlib is available, falls back to ZIP_STORED otherwise.
- Prints the path of the created archive to stdout.

Usage examples
- Create an archive with defaults:
  python3 /workspace/archive_reports.py
- Overwrite an existing archive with the same name:
  python3 /workspace/archive_reports.py --overwrite
- Avoid recursive search (only top-level .txt files):
  python3 /workspace/archive_reports.py --no-recursive
- Use a custom reports or output directory:
  python3 /workspace/archive_reports.py --reports-dir /path/to/reports --output-dir /path/to/archives

