Final report — Secure file archiving implemented and verified

What I implemented
- Created a production-ready script: /workspace/archive_reports.py
  - Finds all .txt files under /workspace/reports (recursive by default).
  - Writes a timestamped zip named reports_<YYYY-MM-DD>.zip into /workspace/archives/.
  - Uses ZIP_DEFLATED when available; falls back to ZIP_STORED.
  - Writes atomically using a temporary file and Path.replace.
  - Skips symlinks (safety).
  - Prints the created archive path to stdout and returns defined exit codes.
  - CLI options: --reports-dir, --output-dir, --date, --no-recursive, --overwrite, --quiet

Security hardening added
- Output directory permissions: 0o700 (rwx------) when created (attempted to set if possible).
- Temporary file permissions: 0o600 (rw-------) where possible.
- Final archive permissions: 0o600 (rw-------) after creation.
- Avoids including symlinks and uses atomic replace to prevent partial archives.

